    "Description": "Migration slice 3 (docs/blueprints/AimAndFireSpecific_Slice_Design.md): blueprint-authored rebuild of the C# oracle HillAttackTankNodes.Action_AimAndFireSpecific (~line 334-438) -- an AiPrimitive BTreeAction. Graph: EventEntry -> GetParameter(TargetNetworkId) -> FunctionCall NetworkEntityMapOps.ResolveTarget(targetNetworkId) [ctx: view, TrailingContext=View, IsPure] -> target Entity, fanned out to WorldOps.IsNull(target) [TrailingContext=None, IsPure] and WorldOps.IsAlive(target) [ctx: view, TrailingContext=View, IsPure] -> BranchNull.True -> Return(Failure); BranchNull.False -> BranchAlive.False -> Return(Success) (target destroyed); BranchAlive.True -> ammo round-count sub-graph: GetComponent(self, WeaponState).Ammo (Target pin unwired => self) + GetVariable(LastObservedAmmo)/GetVariable(RoundsFired)/GetParameter(MaxRounds) feed native Compare (LessThan x2, GreaterThan, GreaterThanOrEqual) + BinaryOp (Subtract, Add) + BooleanOp (And) nodes: BranchA(LastObservedAmmo<0) True -> SetVariable(LastObservedAmmo=ammo) (first-tick init, SHARED merge-point node also reached from the decrement path); False -> BranchB(ammo<LastObservedAmmo) True -> SetVariable(RoundsFired += LastObservedAmmo-ammo) -> the shared SetVariable(LastObservedAmmo=ammo); False -> falls straight through. Both paths converge on BranchCap( (MaxRounds>0) && (RoundsFired>=MaxRounds) ) -- a genuine 2-in-degree merge point, scheduled as a single shared block by the merge-point scheduler fix (no node triplication). BranchCap.True -> Return(Success) (round cap reached, SHARED with the target-destroyed and fire-tail-success returns -- Return is a pure terminal sink, so all three narrative 'Return (Success)' moments in the design doc are the SAME node instance, a 3-in-degree merge point). BranchCap.False -> ChannelCommand(WeaponChannel/AimAndFire) [Target <- resolved target entity, CooldownSeconds <- PinDefault \"10\"] -> WaitForChannel(WeaponChannel) -> the shared Return(Success). DEVIATION 1 (design doc, documented): the oracle's Locomotion-channel clear (stop-to-fire) is DROPPED -- no cross-channel write from this weapon action (architect Q5-B: a brain writes only its own channel via ChannelCommand); the tank is already stationary at its hull-down slot in the real Hill-attack scenario. DEVIATION 2 (design doc, documented): ClearWeaponActionIfActive on the MaxRounds-Success path is SIMPLIFIED to a plain Return(Success) -- the BTree selector/arbitration reclaims the channel (same class as ReverseToBaseline's Clear-on-failure gap). Everything else is faithful to the oracle. New curated helpers: Hrot.AI.Behaviors.Brains.NetworkEntityMapOps.ResolveTarget (P7 context-aware FunctionCall, architect Q6-B target-resolve pattern) and Hrot.AI.Behaviors.Brains.WorldOps.IsAlive/IsNull (general-purpose, broadly reusable). Params vs WorkingState split per Q5-D: MaxRounds/TargetNetworkId = Parameters; RoundsFired/LastObservedAmmo = WorkingState (LastObservedAmmo default -1 sentinel for first-tick init). Does not modify the C# oracle.",
